title: "RSAC: Robotic Surgery Adaptive Curricula"
abstract: >-
  Robotic Surgery Adaptive Curricula (RSAC) is software for generating
  individualised, adaptive training pathways in robotic surgery simulation.
  After each recorded attempt, it evaluates data sufficiency and performance
  trajectories relative to predefined proficiency thresholds, then recommends
  whether the trainee should repeat the current exercise, advance through
  standard or accelerated progression, move to an exercise of comparable
  difficulty, or return to a simpler exercise for remediation. Exercise
  selection follows a predefined curriculum graph that encodes progression,
  lateral moves, and remediation pathways, while retaining proficiency
  requirements for advancement. The distributed version accepts manually
  entered performance metrics and provides the adaptive decision algorithm for
  independent examination, replication, and adaptation to other simulator
  environments.
